# core.autocrlf is true on the dev machine. Git detects binary by scanning for NUL bytes, which a
# zip-based wheel trips — but "usually detected" is a poor guarantee for a file whose corruption
# would surface as an unreadable archive halfway through a Northflank build. Say it outright.
*.whl binary
# A shell script run on a Linux GPU host breaks on CRLF line endings.
*.sh text eol=lf
